{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 456
        },
        "text": "Quad UV, a per-particle random number (pulse phase) and the particle colour / alpha."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_sphere",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2684
        },
        "text": "`r = 2·|uv − ½|` is the distance from the centre (1 at the quad edge). A sphere of radius 1 has `N·V = z = √(1 − r²)` — that is the facing ratio. The halo is `z^haloPower`, the core `z^corePower` (a high power leaves only the centre) and the rim `(1 − z)^rimPower`."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_pulse",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 925
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1766
        },
        "text": "`pulse = 1 + amount · sin(time · speed + random · 2π)` — the random phase keeps several orbs from beating in unison."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_color",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1766
        },
        "text": "`colour = lerp(glow, core, core mask) × (halo + rim) × pulse × intensity × particle colour`. The quad edge is faded with `1 − smoothstep(0.8, 1, r)` so the square never shows."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 5540,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Additive blend, ZWrite off, two-sided. Alpha scales the additive contribution."
      }
    ],
